  "classification": "New classical native-center carrier obstruction via low-factor/two-high-digit averaging, weighted source multiplicities and explicit arbitrary-origin wrap penalty; no query clock improvement",
  "model_authorization": "User authorized parallel Sol 6.1 research; three existing gpt-6.1-sol agents reused.",
  "previous_goal_turn": "Progress: adaptive full-Euclidean carrier obstruction, with native centers outside the previous origin-span regime.",
  "whole_family_soft_linear_query_acquired": false,
  "general_query_bound": "Existing soft O(J+sqrt(JL)), hence soft O(m^(3/2)), unchanged",
  "new_arithmetic_step": "At fixed n, averaging low p and both higher factor digits gives three contributions 2mR^4, 4m^2R^3, 4C^4m^(11/2). The projection (t,a-2u) has at most four labeled triples per fiber. Weighted cone energy handles the last case.",
  "residue_and_selector_bound": "Sum E_mod<=10C^4m^(13/2); bad ordered FACTOR-residue pairs mod m^2<=10m^4/lambda. O(M) integer P lifts per residue and varying-selector Q boxes give O(K_*M^6/lambda); P=Q mod m singular loss O(K_*M^5). Proof-side exceptional set, not public N-only test.",
  "native_center_statement": "Exact midpoint formula cancels centered b; all public/reflected phases lie in a common interval with pair difference<=12m^4+2m^2<16m^4<D. All advised ray/center choices have W=1 without the previous relative-origin-span restriction.",
  "weighted_cover_statement": "At least 2m/3 labeled light tag entries; no distinct-target lower bound asserted. Their weighted energy implies k^2*T>=m^(3/2)/(162*lambda*C^4). Full multicenter packet cover contains a witness, not an asserted full-union energy bound or collision-complete trimmed source.",
  "arbitrary_origin_statement": "For one origin per source entry of span H, V=(m-2)S+6m^2+m^2H and W=2floor(2V/D)+1 give E_global<=W E_mod and the carrier bound divided by W. Off-zero energies<=zero energy by translated Cauchy. Nearlinear few-carrier cover under polylog assumptions requires H>=D/(m^(3/2)polylog m). Numerical span is not a bit-cost lower bound.",
  "original_supply_statement": "Same original Omega(M^6/log^2 M) balanced actual-public-gamma supply. Polylog menus yield soft Omega(m^(3/2)) carrier tradeoff; frozen K_*=O(M^.020), lambda_m=m^.04 yields m^1.46/polylog with O(M^5.980) and O(M^5.020) new losses.",
  "limits": "Not operation lower bound or improved factorization exponent. Tiny advised tag subsets, very wide origins, high-productset carriers, shared operations and implicit scalar queries remain open. Multiple origin copies require separate charge.",
  "verification_scope": "Classical proof with three independent mathematical/source reviews; no new Lean declarations, native edits, examples or broad builds.",
  "missing_work": "Restriction-stable soft O(m) sufficient factor query, all-input and full bit/controller proof, Lean sixth-rate composition.",
